nue), so pricing power is hard to come by."],"mkt":["The shares are roughly flat over the past year excluding the latest month.","The price sits mid-way through its 52-week range, 14% below the high.","With annualised volatility of 33% and a beta of 1.20, it amplifies market moves.","About $45.0M trades a day, enough to build a position.","In past sell-offs it fell 56% in the 2020 crash, 54% in the 2022 bear market and 71% in 2008."],"val":["The stock trades 45% below its DCF fair value of $65.08, a meaningful margin of safety.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 60%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $46.83 to $90.60 (P10-P90), so treat the estimate as noisy.","Multiples send mixed signals against Real Estate peers: cheaper on P/FCF 7.6 vs 17.8, richer on P/E 115.5 vs 23.6 and EV/EBITDA 20.7 vs 16.3 (sector median).","Against its own history it is cheap: the EBIT multiple sits 66% below its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are attractive: an FCF yield of 13.2% (above the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 8.0% (vs the 8% bar).","The 13 covering analysts target $39.23 on average, 10% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 3% falls short of the cost of capital of 10.0%, so growth at these returns destroys value; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 1.09).","It converts 53% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: a Piotroski score of 7/9 and cash conversion of 1.39x.","AFFO margin (a proxy for distributable REIT cash) is 53%.","ROE of 15% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (2.6x equity multiplier).","Operating margin is running 32pp above its own historical average, a peak-margin risk if conditions normalise."],"hlth":["Leverage is conservative at 0.8x net debt to EBITDA ($840.9M of cash against $2.3B of debt), with interest covered 3.7x.","Warning signs: an Altman Z of 0.58 in the distress zone, which caps the rating at HOLD."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 0.2% over 3 years, 3.5% over 5 years and -3.2% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating.","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Free cash flow has compounded 17.8% a year over five years.","Margins are expanding (+2.7% trend).","Forward indicators: FFO growth of 24.3% a year over five years.","Capex runs only 0.6x depreciation (16.4% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown."],"own":["Insiders own 7.4%, meaningful skin in the game, and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insider trading is two-way: 9 purchases and 3 sales over the past year, net $2.2M sold.","It returns 2.6% a year to shareholders (0.7% in buybacks and 2.1% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 0.5% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","It pays out 1850% of earnings, more than it earns, so the dividend is at risk."],"people":["With about 3,145 employees, each generates about $576K of revenue, 0.3x the Real Estate median, and productivity has fallen 2.6% a year.","That works out to $306K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $3.1M (5x revenue per employee).","Stock compensation averages $8K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":68,"head":"Watch: LEAN BUY-rated, but it earns less than its cost of capital.","pros":["Model rating LEAN BUY (composite 50, gates 18/25)","Trades 45% below fair value of $65.08","FCF margin 53.1%","Net debt/EBITDA 0.8x","Piotroski F-score 7/9"],"cons":["ROIC 3.1% vs WACC 10.0%","P/E 115.5x vs sector 23.6x","EV/EBITDA 20.7x vs sector 16.3x"],"flags":[],"need":["it earns less than its cost of capital"],"buy_below":55.32,"vc":{"base":65.08,"base_src":"dcf","bear":46.83,"bull":90.6,"alt_median":27.5,"n_alt":2,"gap":2.5231,"dispersion":0.6031,"level":"LOW","why":["models disagree (60% dispersion)","DCF is 252% above the other models' median ($27.50)"]},"med":{"pe":23.5